      0.466,
      0.867,
      0.623
     ],
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "content": "Research in psychology has suggested that reading fiction can improve individuals' social-cognitive abilities. Findings from neuroscience show that reading and social cognition both recruit the default network, a network which is known to support our capacity to simulate hypothetical scenes, spaces "
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "footer",
