     "bbox": [
      0.121,
      0.38,
      0.488,
      0.516
     ],
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "content": "Follow-up  "
      },
      {
       "type": "equation_inline",
       "content": "2 \\times 2"
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "content": "  repeated-measures ANOVA within subnetworks revealed that the vividness of the passages significantly affected activity in the MTL subnetwork,  "
      },
      {
       "type": "equation_inline",
       "content": "F(1, 25) = 4.38"
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "content": " , P < 0.05, Cohen's d = 0.42, but the presence of people or mental content in the passages had no effect on the MTL subnetwork,  "
      },
      {
       "type": "equation_inline",
       "content": "F(1, 25) = 0.21"
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "content": " , P = 0.65, d = 0.09. This suggests that the MTL network responded most robustly to passages that vividly described scenes but did not differentiate between passages with or without people. No interaction effects between the social and vivid factors were observed,  "
      },
      {
       "type": "equation_inline",
       "content": "F(1, 25) = 2.66"
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "content": " , P = 0.12, partial  "
      },
      {
       "type": "equation_inline",
       "content": "\\eta^{2} = 0.10"
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "content": " ."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
