      {
       "type": "image_caption",
       "index": 13,
       "bbox": [
        0.121,
        0.872,
        0.875,
        0.905
       ],
       "content": [
        {
         "type": "text",
         "content": "Fig 1. BOLD differences for main effect of (A) Social > Non-social (B) Vivid > Abstract, (C) and results of ROI analysis of both contrasts. Both whole-brain and ROI analyses show that the dmPFC subnetwork of the default network responded most robustly to literary passages containing people or mental content, whereas the MTL subnetwork responded most robustly to vivid physical descriptions."
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    }
